{"action": "shared_understanding_confirmed", "at": "2026-08-30T21:49:26+00:00", "data": {"summary": "Bobby confirmed the bounded platform-neutral transfer-list read model. Each query explicitly selects Open or Done for one explicit pool and either one active location or All Locations. One-location scope includes incoming and outgoing transfers; All Locations returns each matching transfer once. Archived endpoints remain out of normal selectors but stay visibly identified when relevant to an active location, while transfers whose endpoints are both archived remain archive-only. Open is urgency-ordered by expected dispatch or arrival; Done is newest terminal event first. Each row is a compact transfer summary with full line, note, actor, receipt, warning, and audit detail left to existing detail reads. Default pagination is 50, maximum 100, with a stable opaque cursor. Search, alternate sorting, GUI, CLI, HTTP/auth, integrations, schema migration, deployment, partial receiving, and Received reversion remain excluded."}, "event_id": "37dda4be-b4b4-4b1c-868a-fcece2bd8d73"}
